 "text": "Hello there! How's everything treating you? It depends on how much it's been used. On an inner tube free bike, at least once a fortnight or after every few days of riding, especially in wet weather. You' pumping on a pump with a pressure gauge, then? You' looking for where the gauge shows the wheel was, then adding about one inch of pressure on top. Squeezing them check if they' fully inflated is a good habit though. Yes, definitely. Turn it way down, then up again when you' finished. Air goes out really fast through the valve.",
